Maybe intelligent pets eat corpses for the same reason the hero does:
not because they like the taste, but because there's a shortage of
proper food in the dungeon, so you'd better eat whatever you can.
However, humanoid non-orc pets should not eat tripe at all, IMHO.
(This is to be consistent with the conditions under which it makes you
sick.  It's possible that the set of monsters which are sickened by
tripe should be changed.  For example, if ogres and trolls count as
humanoid then I think they are sickened by tripe, and perhaps they
shouldn't be.)

The whole concept of training an intelligent pet to fetch with food
rewards doesn't make much sense, but it's not clear what you could
replace it by.  Just ask your pet to walk in and pick up the pile of
stuff you want? :-)
